 "_about": "Two parts. slicePatch (live, unflagged): D1192, the town sign says Fernbrook Trial Hall (maps_slice.json is verbatim design data, so it is overridden here). hallPatch (FLAGGED): the contested Hall, applied by game.js only when HALL2_ON (debug plus ?hall2=1, or HALL2_RELEASED after Vincent's yes; AGENTS rule 9). It runs after fernbrook_rooms.json, so its rows and objects win. Flag off, fb_hall_in is exactly today's room. D1432 (Vincent, Nov 3, 2026): after Seal 1 and the pick the Hall is shut on both paths and keeps the split look until Fen's own Act 2 turn; the Keeper and Glimmerwell looks also need story.fen_turned (additive, set by nothing yet; her turn will set it). D1727 (REPORT_FLAGS default, pending Vincent): the look reads Fen's own turn, story.fen_turned=glimmer / =keepers, not the holder's story.side (under always undercover every holder is a Keeper in public by then). D1434: banners name no colour.",
 "_placeholders": "The lines under hallPatch.addObjs are June's pass (drafted by Claude in June's role, Vincent to approve; Tue Nov 3, 2026), replacing the spec's PLACEHOLDER copy (D1196). No line asks the holder to join a side (D1145).",
